{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matrixorigin/matrixone/pulls/24779","id":3786177332,"node_id":"PR_kwDOFEPiGM7hrHs0","html_url":"https://github.com/matrixorigin/matrixone/pull/24779","diff_url":"https://github.com/matrixorigin/matrixone/pull/24779.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/matrixorigin/matrixone/pull/24779.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matrixorigin/matrixone/issues/24779","number":24779,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(plan): persist and reflect TTL table options (#24552)","user":{"login":"ck89119","id":4971300,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NzEzMDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4971300?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119","html_url":"https://github.com/ck89119","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What type of PR is this?\n\n- [ ] API-change\n- [ ] BUG\n- [ ] Improvement\n- [ ] Documentation\n- [x] Feature\n- [ ] Test and CI\n- [ ] Code Refactoring\n\n## Which issue(s) this PR fixes:\n\nissue #24552\n\n> **PR 2 of a multi-PR series** for native table-level TTL. **Depends on #24754**\n> (parser layer). Until #24754 merges, this PR's diff also contains the parser\n> commits from #24754 — please review only the plan-layer commit here, or review\n> after #24754 is merged (the diff will then reduce to PR-2 only). Does not close\n> the issue.\n\n## What this PR does / why we need it:\n\nSecond step of native table-level TTL: persist the TTL table options into the\ntable metadata on `CREATE TABLE`, and reflect them back in `SHOW CREATE TABLE`.\n\n### Changes\n\n- `buildCreateTable` (`build_ddl.go`): validate and persist `TTL` /\n  `TTL_ENABLE` / `TTL_JOB_INTERVAL` as table properties\n  (`rel_ttl` / `rel_ttl_enable` / `rel_ttl_job_interval`), reusing the same\n  property mechanism as `COMMENT`. Defaults are applied (`enable=on`,\n  `job_interval=1h`). Invalid usage is rejected:\n  - TTL column must exist and be `DATE` / `DATETIME` / `TIMESTAMP`\n  - `TTL_JOB_INTERVAL` must be a positive duration (e.g. `1h`, `30m`)\n  - `TTL_ENABLE` must be `on` / `off`\n  - `TTL_ENABLE` / `TTL_JOB_INTERVAL` without a `TTL` expression is an error\n  - TTL is rejected on temporary / cluster / dynamic / external tables\n- `ConstructCreateTableSQL` (`build_show_util.go`): reflect the TTL clause,\n  round-trippable through the parser; the TTL keys are excluded from the\n  generic `PROPERTIES()` clause.\n- `ttl_util.go`: TTL expression / option validation helpers.\n- `pkg/catalog/types.go`: new `SystemRelAttr_TTL*` property-key constants.\n- Tests: validation, persistence with defaults, error cases, and\n  `SHOW CREATE TABLE` round-trip.\n\n### Scope / safety\n\n`ALTER TABLE ... TTL` is still rejected as not-supported (lands in a later PR),\nas is the background expiry job. No behavior change for tables without TTL.\n\n`make`, `make static-check` and `go test ./pkg/sql/plan/...` all pass.","created_at":"2026-06-02T07:00:26Z","updated_at":"2026-07-23T07:48:35Z","closed_at":"2026-07-23T07:48:35Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"XuPeng-SH","id":39627130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NjI3MTMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39627130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH","html_url":"https://github.com/XuPeng-SH","fol